:HELP NAME=ANZPRB.Analyze Problem (ANZPRB)
:P.Use the Analyze Problem (ANZPRB) command to guided analysis of a
problem the user saw; the questions are panels, so a display is needed.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ANZPRB/ANZTYPE'.Type of analysis (ANZTYPE)
:P.The type of analysis for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MENU.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGCNTINF.Change Contact Information (CHGCNTINF)
:P.Use the Change Contact Information (CHGCNTINF) command to who the
service provider reaches, and where.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCNTINF/CMPNY'.Company (CMPNY)
:P.The company for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 36 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCNTINF/CONTACT'.Contact (CONTACT)
:P.The contact for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 36 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCNTINF/TELNBR'.Telephone number (TELNBR)
:P.The telephone number for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Primary
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Alternative
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCNTINF/FAXTELNBR'.Fax telephone number (FAXTELNBR)
:P.The fax telephone number for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Primary
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Alternative
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCNTINF/MAILADDR'.Mailing address (MAILADDR)
:P.The mailing address for this command.
:P.The value has 4 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Street address
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 36 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. City/State
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 36 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Country or region
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 20 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 4&colon. Postal code
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 12 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCNTINF/LNGVER'.National language version (LNGVER)
:P.The national language version for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCNTINF/MEDPTF'.Media for mailing fixes (MEDPTF)
:P.The media for mailing fixes for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTOMATIC, *OPTICAL, *TAPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGCNTINF/EMAIL'.E-mail address (EMAIL)
:P.The e-mail address for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGPRB.Change Problem (CHGPRB)
:P.Use the Change Problem (CHGPRB) command to change a logged problem.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRB/PRBID'.Problem identifier (PRBID)
:P.The problem identifier, as WRKPRB shows it.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRB/SEV'.Severity (SEV)
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRB/ASSIGNTO'.Assigned to (ASSIGNTO)
:P.The assigned to for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRB/STATUS'.Status (STATUS)
:P.The status for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPENED, *READY, *PREPARED, *SENT, *ANSWERED,
*VERIFIED, *CLOSED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPRB/TEXT'.Note text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 70 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTPRB.Delete Problem (DLTPRB)
:P.Use the Delete Problem (DLTPRB) command to delete problems from the
problem log.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTPRB/PRBID'.Problem identifier (PRBID)
:P.The problem identifier, as WRKPRB shows it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTPRB/STATUS'.Status (STATUS)
:P.The status for this command.
:P.Up to 7 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPENED, *READY, *PREPARED, *SENT, *ANSWERED,
*VERIFIED, *CLOSED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTPRB/DAYS'.Days old (DAYS)
:P.The days old for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DMPJOB.Dump Job (DMPJOB)
:P.The Dump Job (DMPJOB) command works with the job's call stack,
variables and storage to QPSRVDMP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DMPJOB/PGMSTG'.Program storage (PGMSTG)
:P.The program storage for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DMPJOB/JOBARA'.Job areas (JOBARA)
:P.The job areas for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*MIN:EPK.
:PD.The smallest value.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DMPJOB/JOBTHDSET'.Job thread set (JOBTHDSET)
:P.The job thread set for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *THDID.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DMPOBJ.Dump Object (DMPOBJ)
:P.The Dump Object (DMPOBJ) command works with a formatted dump of an
object to QPSRVDMP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DMPOBJ/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DMPOBJ/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DMPSYSOBJ.Dump System Object (DMPSYSOBJ)
:P.The Dump System Object (DMPSYSOBJ) command works with a formatted
dump of a system object by name and type, or by its object identifier,
to QPSRVDMP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DMPSYSOBJ/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 40 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DMPSYSOBJ/CONTEXT'.Context (CONTEXT)
:P.The context for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSYS is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DMPSYSOBJ/TYPE'.Object type (TYPE)
:P.The object type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DMPSYSOBJ/SUBTYPE'.Object subtype (SUBTYPE)
:P.The object subtype for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPPRB.Display Problems (DSPPRB)
:P.Use the Display Problems (DSPPRB) command to show logged problems in
detail, or print the problem log report.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/PRBID'.Problem identifier (PRBID)
:P.The problem identifier, as WRKPRB shows it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/STATUS'.Status type (STATUS)
:P.The status type for this command.
:P.Up to 7 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPENED, *READY, *PREPARED, *SENT, *ANSWERED,
*VERIFIED, *CLOSED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/SEV'.Severity (SEV)
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.The value must be 1, 2, 3, 4.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/PERIOD'.Period (PERIOD)
:P.The period for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Start time and date
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Start time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AVAIL:EPK.
:PD.Every available one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Start date
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BEGIN.
:H4.Part 2&colon. End time and date
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. End time
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AVAIL:EPK.
:PD.Every available one.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. End date
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/HARDWARE'.Hardware (HARDWARE)
:P.The hardware for this command.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Device type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Model number
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Serial number
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/RESOURCE'.Resource name (RESOURCE)
:P.The resource name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, QS00SS1
for example.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Program identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Release
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Modification level
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/FUNCTION'.Function (FUNCTION)
:P.The function for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/ORIGIN'.Origin (ORIGIN)
:P.The origin for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Network identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Control point name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/SRVID'.Service number (SRVID)
:P.The service number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 20 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/BRANCH'.Branch number (BRANCH)
:P.The branch number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/COUNTRY'.Country or region number (COUNTRY)
:P.The country or region number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/ASNUSER'.User assigned (ASNUSER)
:P.The user assigned for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/GROUP'.Group assigned (GROUP)
:P.The group assigned for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/PRBTYPE'.Problem type (PRBTYPE)
:P.The problem type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/PRBCGY'.Problem category (PRBCGY)
:P.The problem category for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPRB/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPSRVSTS.Display Service Status (DSPSRVSTS)
:P.Use the Display Service Status (DSPSRVSTS) command to whether a job
is serviced, traced or debugged.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSRVSTS/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSRVSTS/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDTRC.End Trace (ENDTRC)
:P.Use the End Trace (ENDTRC) command to end a trace session, keeping or
deleting its data.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTRC/SSNID'.Session ID (SSNID)
:P.The session ID for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTRC/DTAOPT'.Data option (DTAOPT)
:P.The data option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DLT:EPK.
:PD.Delete authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTRC/DTALIB'.Data library (DTALIB)
:P.The data library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QGPL is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTRC/REPLACE'.Replace data (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTRC/PRTTRC'.Print trace data (PRTTRC)
:P.Whether to print trace data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PRTTRC.Print Trace Data (PRTTRC)
:P.Use the Print Trace Data (PRTTRC) command to print trace data ENDTRC
kept.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTTRC/DTAMBR'.Data member (DTAMBR)
:P.The data member for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTTRC/DTALIB'.Data library (DTALIB)
:P.The data library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QGPL is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTTRC/DLTTRC'.Delete trace (DLTTRC)
:P.Whether to delete trace.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RCLDBXREF.Reclaim DB Cross-Reference (RCLDBXREF)
:P.Use the Reclaim DB Cross-Reference (RCLDBXREF) command to check, or
put right, the database cross-reference.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLDBXREF/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CHECK, *FIX.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCLDBXREF/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ERR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDSRVRQS.Send Service Request (SNDSRVRQS)
:P.Use the Send Service Request (SNDSRVRQS) command to test the
connection to the service provider.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSRVRQS/ACTION'.Action (ACTION)
:P.The action for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TEST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSRVRQS/RMTCPNAME'.Remote control point (RMTCPNAME)
:P.The remote control point for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IBMSRV.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSRVRQS/RMTNETID'.Remote network identifier (RMTNETID)
:P.The network identifier of the remote location.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDSRVRQS/CNNTYPE'.Connection type (CNNTYPE)
:P.The connection type for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTOMATIC, *DIRECT, *IPCNN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRTRC.Start Trace (STRTRC)
:P.Use the Start Trace (STRTRC) command to start a job trace session.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTRC/SSNID'.Session ID (SSNID)
:P.The session ID for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTRC/JOB'.Jobs (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTRC/MAXSTG'.Maximum storage to use (MAXSTG)
:P.The most auxiliary storage, in kilobytes, the user's objects may
occupy.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4000000.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 10000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTRC/TRCFULL'.Trace full (TRCFULL)
:P.The trace full for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:PT.:PK.*STOPTRC:EPK.
:PD.When full, the trace stops.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTRC/JOBTRCTYPE'.Job trace type (JOBTRCTYPE)
:P.The job trace type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FLOW, *DATA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=TRCINT.Trace Internal (TRCINT)
:P.Use the Trace Internal (TRCINT) command to start, stop and list the
system's internal trace points, for problem analysis with your service
provider.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCINT/SET'.Trace option setting (SET)
:P.The trace option setting for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ON:EPK.
:PD.On.
:PT.:PK.*OFF:EPK.
:PD.Off.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PK.*HOLD:EPK.
:PD.Held.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCINT/TRCTBL'.Trace table (TRCTBL)
:P.The trace table for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QSTRCTBL is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCINT/SIZE'.Trace table size (SIZE)
:P.The trace table size for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 512000.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1024 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCINT/TRCFULL'.Trace full (TRCFULL)
:P.The trace full for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:PT.:PK.*STOPTRC:EPK.
:PD.When full, the trace stops.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCINT/TRCTYPE'.Trace type (TRCTYPE)
:P.The trace type for this command.
:P.Up to 9 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CMD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the command.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PK.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CALL, *REQ, *IO, *PRB, *DMP, *LOG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCINT/JOBNBR'.Job number (JOBNBR)
:P.The job number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=TRCJOB.Trace Job (TRCJOB)
:P.The Trace Job (TRCJOB) command works with the older job trace,
switched on and off in the job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCJOB/SET'.Trace option setting (SET)
:P.The trace option setting for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ON:EPK.
:PD.On.
:PT.:PK.*OFF:EPK.
:PD.Off.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCJOB/TRCTYPE'.Trace type (TRCTYPE)
:P.The trace type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FLOW, *DATA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCJOB/MAXSTG'.Maximum storage to use (MAXSTG)
:P.The most auxiliary storage, in kilobytes, the user's objects may
occupy.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16000.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 16000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCJOB/TRCFULL'.Trace full (TRCFULL)
:P.The trace full for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*WRAP:EPK.
:PD.When full, the oldest entries are overwritten.
:PT.:PK.*STOPTRC:EPK.
:PD.When full, the trace stops.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TRCJOB/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKCNTINF.Work with Contact Information (WRKCNTINF)
:P.The Work with Contact Information (WRKCNTINF) command works with the
support contact information menu.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKPRB.Work with Problems (WRKPRB)
:P.Use the Work with Problems (WRKPRB) command to list the problems the
system logged (none are logged yet).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPRB/PRBID'.Problem identifier (PRBID)
:P.The problem identifier, as WRKPRB shows it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPRB/STATUS'.Status (STATUS)
:P.The status for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPENED, *READY, *PREPARED, *SENT, *ANSWERED,
*VERIFIED, *CLOSED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSRVPVD.Work with Service Providers (WRKSRVPVD)
:P.The Work with Service Providers (WRKSRVPVD) command works with the
service providers this system reports to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSRVPVD/CNNTYPE'.Connection type (CNNTYPE)
:P.The connection type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DIRECT, *IPCNN.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
